mmands required to install the dependencies and start the uvicorn development server.\n\nConstraints: Do not write any frontend code or create frontend folders yet. Focus exclusively on the backend setup"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "**Terminal commands**\n\n```powershell\n# 1. Move into the new backend folder\ncd c:\\Users\\mohit\\Desktop\\python\\TESTING_VERTEX_SWARM\\backend\n\n# 2. Install the required packages (FastAPI and Uvicorn)\npython -m pip install -r requirements.txt\n\n# 3. Start the FastAPI development server\nuvicorn main:app --reload\n```"}, {"role": "user", "content": "i want you to use these cmds but you forgot to create venv which is mandatory + then install req and start server as it happens in any prod app"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "**Terminal commands (including virtual‑environment creation)**\n\n```powershell\n# 1️⃣ Create a virtual‑environment inside the backend folder\ncd c:\\Users\\mohit\\Desktop\\python\\TESTING_VERTEX_SWARM\\backend\npython -m venv venv\n\n# 2️⃣ Activate the virtual‑environment\n#    (PowerShell syntax – use the same terminal where you’ll run the next commands)\n.\\venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1\n\n# 3️⃣ Upgrade pip (optional but recommended)\npython -m pip install --upgrade pip\n\n# 4️⃣ Install the project dependencies from requirements.txt\npython -m pip install -r requirements.txt\n\n# 5️⃣ Start the FastAPI development server with hot‑reload\nuvicorn main:app --reload\n```\n\nThese steps create an isolated `venv`, install **fastapi** and **uvicorn** into it, and then launch the API server as you would in a production‑ready development workflow."}, {"role": "user", "content": "why are you giving me terminals cmd here ?and not doin g it yourseld?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The backend is now fully set up:\n\n1. **Virtual environment** created and activated (`venv`).\n2. **Dependencies** (`fastapi`, `uvicorn`) installed from `requirements.txt`.\n3. **FastAPI app** (`backend/main.py`) already contai