T http://localhost:8000/api/increment/`.  \n   - On success the UI updates with the new counter value (e.g., `1`, `2`, …).  \n\nIf the counter does not change:\n\n- Open the **Developer Tools → Network** tab in the browser.  \n- Confirm that the request to `http://localhost:8000/api/increment/` returns **200 OK** with a JSON payload like `{\"value\": 3}`.  \n- If you still see a **404**, double‑check that the backend is running (step 1) and that the URL matches exactly (including the trailing slash).  \n\n---\n\n## 4️⃣ Quick “one‑liner” script (optional)\n\nIf you prefer a single PowerShell window that launches both services in parallel, you can run:\n\n```powershell\n# From the repository root (C:\\Users\\mohit\\Desktop\\python\\TESTING_VERTEX_SWARM)\nStart-Process -FilePath \"powershell\" -ArgumentList \"-NoProfile -Command `\"cd .\\backend; .\\venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1; uvicorn main:app --reload`\"\"\nStart-Process -FilePath \"powershell\" -ArgumentList \"-NoProfile -Command `\"cd .\\frontend; npm install; npm run dev`\"\"\n```\n\nEach `Start-Process` opens a new PowerShell window with the appropriate service running.\n\n---\n\n### TL;DR Commands (copy‑paste)\n\n```powershell\n# ── Backend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ncd C:\\Users\\mohit\\Desktop\\python\\TESTING_VERTEX_SWARM\\backend\n.\\venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1        # <-- optional, activates venv\npip install -r requirements.txt   # <-- only first time / after changes\nuvicorn main:app --reload\n\n# ── Frontend ────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ncd C:\\Users\\mohit\\Desktop\\python\\TESTING_VERTEX_SWARM\\frontend\nnpm install                        # <-- only first time / after changes\nnpm run dev\n```\n\nRun the backend first, then the frontend. After both are up, the **Increment** button should work correctly."}, {"role": "user", "content": "PS C:\\Users\\mohit\\Desktop\\python\\TESTING_VERTEX_SWARM> .\\venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1 \n.\\venv\\Scripts\\Activa