em with **curl** (or PowerShell’s `Invoke-WebRequest`):\n\n```powershell\n# Get current value\ncurl http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/value/\n\n# Increment\ncurl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/increment/\n```\n\nBoth should return JSON with a numeric `value`.\n\n---\n\n## 2️⃣ Frontend – Next JS (React)\n\n| Step | Action | Command |\n|------|--------|---------|\n| **a.** | Open another PowerShell terminal (or split the current one) and **cd** into the frontend folder | ```powershell\\ncd C:\\Users\\mohit\\Desktop\\python\\TESTING_VERTEX_SWARM\\frontend\\n``` |\n| **b.** | Install the Node dependencies (only the first time or after editing `package.json`) | ```powershell\\nnpm install\\n``` |\n| **c.** | **Start the development server** – it will start on `http://localhost:3000` by default | ```powershell\\nnpm run dev\\n``` |\n\n*What you’ll see:*  \n\n```\n> frontend@ dev\n> next dev\n\nready - compiled successfully\n✔  Production ready at http://localhost:3000\n```\n\nThe page will automatically reload whenever you edit source files.\n\n---\n\n## 3️⃣ Verify End‑to‑End\n\n1. Open a browser and navigate to **http://localhost:3000**.  \n2. You should see the Counter UI (the component `Counter.jsx`).  \n3. Click the **“Increment”** button.  \n   - The button triggers a `POST http://localhost:8000/api/increment/`.  \n   - On success the UI updates with the new counter value (e.g., `1`, `2`, …).  \n\nIf the counter does not change:\n\n- Open the **Developer Tools → Network** tab in the browser.  \n- Confirm that the request to `http://localhost:8000/api/increment/` returns **200 OK** with a JSON payload like `{\"value\": 3}`.  \n- If you still see a **404**, double‑check that the backend is running (step 1) and that the URL matches exactly (including the trailing slash).  \n\n---\n\n## 4️⃣ Quick “one‑liner” script (optional)\n\nIf you prefer a single PowerShell window that launches both services in parallel, you can run:\n\n```powershell\n# From the repository root (C:\\User