unning. Track its PID with `list_processes`.\n\nWorkspace Root: provided by extension host\n\nProject Structure:\nTESTING_VERTEX_SWARM/\n  .agents/\n  .git/ [collapsed]\n  backend/\n    __pycache__/\n    main.py\n    requirements.txt\n    venv/\n  frontend/\n    .git/\n    .gitignore\n    .next/\n    AGENTS.md\n    app/\n      components/\n        Counter.jsx\n      layout.jsx\n      page.jsx\n    CLAUDE.md\n    next-env.d.ts\n    next.config.ts\n    node_modules/\n    package-lock.json\n    package.json\n    pages/\n      _app.tsx\n      _document.tsx\n      api/\n        hello.ts\n      old_index.tsx\n    postcss.config.mjs\n    public/\n      favicon.ico\n      file.svg\n      globe.svg\n      next.svg\n      vercel.svg\n      window.svg\n    README.md\n    styles/\n      globals.css\n    tsconfig.json\n[collapsed] folders exist but are intentionally not expanded."}, {"role": "system", "content": "VS Code request context:\nActive file: c:\\Users\\mohit\\Desktop\\python\\TESTING_VERTEX_SWARM\\backend\\main.py\nLanguage: python\nActive terminal: Vertex Worker\nTerminal shell: C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe\nOperating System: win32\nWorkspace folders:\n- c:\\Users\\mohit\\Desktop\\python\\TESTING_VERTEX_SWARM"}, {"role": "user", "content": "what is cmd to run backend"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "203f14da-8fc6-4535-88f1-9cceec3589d4", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "load_tool_context", "arguments": "{\"categories\":[\"workspace_ops\",\"terminal_ops\"]}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "203f14da-8fc6-4535-88f1-9cceec3589d4", "content": "{\"status\": \"success\", \"content\": \"Tool guidance loaded for: workspace_ops, terminal_ops.\\n\\n## WORKSPACE OPERATIONS TOOL GUIDANCE\\n\\n> **TOOL NAME IS EXACTLY `workspace_ops`**. The JSON key must be `\\\"tool_name\\\": \\\"workspace_ops\\\"`. Any other string will be rejected with a DEPRECATED_TOOL error.\\n\\nworkspace_ops is the single source of truth for all file system operations.\\nEvery call requires: action, request_id, mode, payload.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### HASH-BASED CONCURRENCY PROTOCOL (MANDATORY)\\n\\nYour mutations MUST include `expected_hash`. This is your contract with the file system.\\n\\n**STEP 1: READ THE FILE(S)**\\nDetermine your reading strategy based on the overall objective. Sequential reading (one-by-one) is slow and inefficient.\\n\\n*Option A: Bulk File Read (`bulk_files_read`) — **RECOMMENDED FOR SPEED***\\n- Use when: Your overall task objective implies you will need the context of multiple files. Since you already have the folder structure, group your reads together to minimize latency.\\n- Flexibility & Limits: You are heavily encouraged to batch your file reads in intelligent batches (up to 5 files at once). The total batch has a 100KB limit; if exceeded, the result is truncated, so group files strategically.\\n- Action: `bulk_files_read`, mode: `preview`, payload: `{ paths: [\\\"path/1.py\\\", \\\"path/2.py\\\"] }`\\n- Hash Handling: The response contains an array at `data.files`. EACH file object contains its own `current_hash`. Map the hash to the specific file for editing.\\n\\n*Option B: Single File Read (`read_file`)*\\n- Use when: You are **certain** that you need only ONE specific file for the overall objective, or you need to paginate through a single massive file that would otherwise break the 100KB bulk limit.\\n- Action: `read_file`, mode: `preview`, payload: `{ path, startLine?, endLine? }`\\n- Hash Handling: The response JSON contains `data.current_hash`. Extract and save this hash.\\n\\n- CRITICAL: A `current_hash` is ALWAYS present in a successful read response. Do NOT use a placeholder. Do NOT skip this step. Do NOT proceed to edit without a real hash string.\\n\\n**STEP 2: PLAN YOUR EDIT**\\n- Decide what to change. Keep the exact hash string in memory — you will paste it verbatim.\\n\\n**STEP 3: APPLY THE EDIT**\\n- Call workspace_ops with action: `edit_file`,