n```jsx\n      const data = await res.json();\n      setCount(data.value);\n    } catch (e) {\n      console.error(\"Failed to increment\", e);\n      setError(\"Couldn't increment the counter.\");\n    }\n  };\n```\nThis code was floating outside any function, causing `'try' expected` and `Declaration or statement expected` errors.\n\n**Fix:** Removed the orphaned 5-line block.\n\n---\n\n### 2. `backend/main.py` — Duplicate increment endpoint with missing decorator (lines 34-37)\n**Problem:** There was a duplicate `/api/increment` endpoint that was missing the `@app` decorator prefix:\n```python\n.post(\"/api/increment\")          # ← missing @app\nasync def increment_trailing():\n    counter.value += 1\n    return {\"value\": counter.value}\n```\nThis caused `Expected expression` error and was a redundant duplicate of the existing `increment_counter` function.\n\n**Fix:** Removed the entire duplicate function (4 lines).\n\n---\n\nBoth files now pass syntax checks and VS Code diagnostics are completely clean. ✅"}, {"role": "user", "content": "PS C:\\Users\\mohit\\Desktop\\python\\TESTING_VERTEX_SWARM> \nPS C:\\Users\\mohit\\Desktop\\python\\TESTING_VERTEX_SWARM> cd frontend                                                                           \nPS C:\\Users\\mohit\\Desktop\\python\\TESTING_VERTEX_SWARM\\frontend> npm run dev\n\n> frontend@0.1.0 dev\n> next dev\n\n▲ Next.js 16.2.9 (Turbopack)\n- Local:         http://localhost:3000\n- Network:       http://192.168.31.33:3000\n✓ Ready in 51s\n\n○ Compiling / ...\n GET /sw.js 404 in 10.1s (next.js: 8.2s, application-code: 1840ms)\n GET / 404 in 10.6s (next.js: 9.8s, application-code: 808ms)\n GET /sw.js 404 in 451ms (next.js: 36ms, application-code: 415ms)\n GET / 404 in 462ms (next.js: 249ms, application-code: 214ms)\n GET /sw.js 404 in 210ms (next.js: 27ms, application-code: 183ms)\n GET / 404 in 538ms (next.js: 34ms, application-code: 504ms)\n GET /sw.js 404 in 819ms (next.js: 31ms, application-code: 788ms)"}, 