e level (since the includes don't cover `.jsx`), but Next.js App Router routing doesn't recognize `.jsx` in `app/` at all — only `.tsx`/`.ts`/`.js`.** That's why `GET /` is 404 — `page.jsx` isn't being picked up.\n\n**2. `page.jsx` (line 28):** File is named `page.jsx` but Next.js App Router requires `.tsx` for JSX files. The `tsconfig.json` includes `**/*.ts` and `**/*.tsx` but **not** `.jsx`. So Next.js is not routing `app/page.jsx` → `/`.\n\nLet me fix both now.\n\n**Fix 1:** Rename `page.jsx` → `page.tsx`", "tool_calls": [{"id": "224078f7-36c5-4e02-9d5b-bfa2997b2599", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "workspace_ops", "arguments": "{\"action\":\"rename_path\",\"mode\":\"apply\",\"payload\":{\"newPath\":\"frontend/app/page.tsx\",\"oldPath\":\"frontend/app/page.jsx\"},\"request_id\":\"rename_page_jsx_to_tsx\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "224078f7-36c5-4e02-9d5b-bfa2997b2599", "content": "{\"status\": \"error\", \"content\": \"rename_path requires expected_hash or expected_version before apply.\", \"error_code\": \"MISSING_CONCURRENCY_GUARD\", \"data\": {\"request_id\": \"rename_page_jsx_to_tsx\", \"action\": \"rename_path\", \"mode\": \"apply\"}, \"conflict\": {\"target\": \"frontend/app/page.jsx\", \"expected_hash\": null, \"expected_version\": null, \"current_version\": \"fnv1a-a000d304-1108\"}}"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "f100b6d6-d0c5-409f-84bb-5c90129e53f4", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "workspace_ops", "arguments": "{\"action\":\"rename_path\",\"mode\":\"apply\",\"payload\":{\"expected_hash\":\"fnv1a-a000d304-1108\",\"newPath\":\"frontend/app/page.tsx\",\"oldPath\":\"frontend/app/page.jsx\"},\"request_id\":\"rename_page_jsx_to_tsx\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "f100b6d6-d0c5-409f-84bb-5c90129e53f4", "content": "{\"status\": \"success\", \"content\": \"{\\n  \\\"action\\\": \\\"rename_path\\\",\\n  \\\"mode\\\": \\\"apply\\\",\\n  \\\"request_id\\\": \\\"rename_page_jsx_to_tsx\\\"