s/Counter\\\";\\n\\nexport default function Home() {\\n  return (\\n    <main className=\\\"min-h-screen bg-[radial-gradient(circle_at_top,_#1f2937_0,_#0f172a_45%,_#020617_100%)] px-6 py-12 text-white\\\">\\n      <div className=\\\"mx-auto flex w-full max-w-4xl flex-col gap-8\\\">\\n        <header className=\\\"space-y-4\\\">\\n          <p className=\\\"inline-flex rounded-full border border-cyan-400/30 bg-cyan-400/10 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-cyan-200\\\">\\n            Frontend Health Check\\n          </p>\\n          <h1 className=\\\"max-w-2xl text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-6xl\\\">\\n            Tailwind is alive, and we can see the API state clearly.\\n          </h1>\\n          <p className=\\\"max-w-2xl text-sm leading-7 text-slate-300 sm:text-base\\\">\\n            If this card styling appears, the Tailwind pipeline is working.\\n            If the counter still fails to load, the issue is in the API port or\\n            request logic rather than CSS.\\n          </p>\\n        </header>\\n\\n        <Counter />\\n      </div>\\n    </main>\\n  );\\n}\\n\", \"current_hash\": \"fnv1a-a000d304-1108\", \"total_lines\": 28, \"status\": \"success\"}, {\"path\": \"frontend/app/layout.jsx\", \"content\": \"import \\\"../styles/globals.css\\\";\\n\\nexport default function RootLayout({ children }) {\\n  return (\\n    <html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n      <body>{children}</body>\\n    </html>\\n  );\\n}\\n\", \"current_hash\": \"fnv1a-f74defea-165\", \"total_lines\": 10, \"status\": \"success\"}], \"truncated\": false}}"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The `page.jsx` and `layout.jsx` look fine. The issue is the **file extension** — Next.js App Router requires `.tsx` or `.js` but `.jsx` might not be resolving properly. Also, the `Counter.jsx` needs checking. Let me also look at the `next.config.ts` and check the `Counter` component.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "a79eacdc-5580-4b3e-88a5-3fb9131c9bb4", "ty