a485-2937db66ebdd", "content": "{\"status\": \"success\", \"content\": \"from fastapi import FastAPI\\nfrom fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware\\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\\nimport uvicorn\\n\\napp = FastAPI()\\n\\napp.add_middleware(\\n    CORSMiddleware,\\n    allow_origins=[\\\"http://localhost:3000\\\", \\\"http://127.0.0.1:3000\\\"],\\n    allow_credentials=True,\\n    allow_methods=[\\\"*\\\"],\\n    allow_headers=[\\\"*\\\"],\\n)\\n\\n@app.get(\\\"/\\\")\\nasync def root():\\n    return {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Backend is running!\\\"}\\n\\nclass Counter(BaseModel):\\n    value: int = 0\\n\\ncounter = Counter()\\n\\n@app.get(\\\"/api/value\\\")\\nasync def get_value():\\n    return {\\\"value\\\": counter.value}\\n\\n@app.post(\\\"/api/increment\\\")\\nasync def increment_counter():\\n    counter.value += 1\\n    return {\\\"value\\\": counter.value}\\n\\n\\n@app.post(\\\"/api/decrement\\\")\\nasync def decrement_counter():\\n    counter.value -= 1\\n    return {\\\"value\\\": counter.value}\\n\\n@app.post(\\\"/api/reset\\\") \\nasync def reset_counter():\\n    counter.value = 0\\n    return {\\\"value\\\": counter.value}\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    uvicorn.run(\\\"main:app\\\", host=\\\"127.0.0.1\\\", port=9000, reload=True)\\n\", \"data\": {\"path\": \"backend/main.py\", \"startLine\": 1, \"endLine\": 200, \"total_lines\": 48, \"current_hash\": \"fnv1a-9081878c-1011\"}}"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I have a clear picture. Here are **all the issues** I found:\n\n---\n\n### Issues Found\n\n**1. `Counter.jsx` (lines 50-53):** Orphaned leaked code after the `increment` function ends — literal lines of code are floating outside any function:\n```\n      const data = await res.json();\n      setCount(data.value);\n;\n\n```\nThis is invalid JavaScript outside a function — the `const data = await res.json()` and `setCount(data.value);` lines are dangling. **The dev server may still compile this file successfully at the fil